24. Single Number
Easy
Pattern: Arrays · Bit manipulation · XOR
Every element in an array appears exactly twice except for one element, which appears once. Find that element.
Example: nums = [4, 1, 2, 1, 2]
Output: 4
Explanation: 1 and 2 each appear twice; 4 appears only once.


Solution:

const nums = [4, 1, 2, 1, 2];
const map = new Map();
let single;

for (let i = 0; i < nums.length; i++) {
  if (!map.has(nums[i])) {
    map.set(nums[i], 1);
  } else {
    map.set(nums[i], map.get(nums[i]) + 1);
  }
}

for (let [key, value] of map) {
  if (value === 1) {
    single = key;
    break;
  }
}

console.log(single);
